      "headline": "Trump renews effort to fire Fed’s Lisa Cook despite Supreme Court ruling",
      "confirmed_facts": [
        {
          "fact_id": "f1",
          "text": "The White House told Cook in a letter this week that the president was “considering” removing her from her role and demanded she respond to unproven mortgage fraud allegations within three weeks – allegations her lawyer called “baseless”.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-08T08:03:08.391904+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "60823a9a86c4d041e73d715f71c81db9a17dfe01dce47fba9b0117d78d7de230",
          "excerpt": "The White House told Cook in a letter this week that the president was “considering” removing her from her role and demanded she respond to unproven mortgage fraud allegations within three weeks – allegations her lawyer called “baseless”.",
          "sentence_hash": "c923af2f71966728c2964b5bf1052893dda1b19f772787ab0e6de2ecee67e59d",
          "anchors": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f2",
          "text": "Trump earlier this week also issued another order attempting to limit birthright citizenship after the high court ruled against his previous effort to limit who is automatically considered a US citizen.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-08T08:03:08.391963+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "60823a9a86c4d041e73d715f71c81db9a17dfe01dce47fba9b0117d78d7de230",
          "excerpt": "Trump earlier this week also issued another order attempting to limit birthright citizenship after the high court ruled against his previous effort to limit who is automatically considered a US citizen.",
          "sentence_hash": "91b413f332b0c29228eee2ba64fac157900a28c714c8b485c6de1532820017dc",
          "anchors": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f3",
          "text": "The letter to Cook, signed by Deputy Chief of Staff Dan Scavino and first reported by ABC News, alleged that she committed crimes that could be punishable by up to 30 years in prison and that her conduct constituted negligence that called into question her trustworthiness as a Fe",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-08T08:03:08.392003+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "60823a9a86c4d041e73d715f71c81db9a17dfe01dce47fba9b0117d78d7de230",
          "excerpt": "The letter to Cook, signed by Deputy Chief of Staff Dan Scavino and first reported by ABC News, alleged that she committed crimes that could be punishable by up to 30 years in prison and that her conduct constituted negligence that called into question her trustworthiness as a Fe",
          "sentence_hash": "bf697d013c55a885f13b7a66a71b014992d017236925967ce8bd51427b293fbe",
          "anchors": [
            "us"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f4",
          "text": "In a statement, Cook’s lawyer said “there is no valid cause” for removing Cook from her position.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-08T08:03:08.392021+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "60823a9a86c4d041e73d715f71c81db9a17dfe01dce47fba9b0117d78d7de230",
          "excerpt": "In a statement, Cook’s lawyer said “there is no valid cause” for removing Cook from her position.",
          "sentence_hash": "1c5413d8b3a127778671d0d01e8bf0dbfbbd30338146652be07085f2430341fe",
          "anchors": [
            "us"
          ]
        }
